				<p>Jakarta, Indonesia -  XX October 2020 – To commemorate Global Handwashing Day on October 15, Ecolab together with Danone-AQUA launches "Hand Hygiene for All," a campaign bringing hand hygiene awareness and products to districts and villages across Indonesia. </p>
				<p>In this time of COVID-19, good hand hygiene is one of the simplest ways to prevent disease transmission. </p>
				<p>According to data from the World Health Organization (WHO), three billion people (40% of the global population) have no means of handwashing with soap and water at home. Based on a recent survey in Indonesia last September from Badan Pusat Statistik (BPS), only 75% of  90,967 respondents indicated compliance with handwashing guidelines. These numbers reflect an unfamiliarity with the importance of basic handwashing among the general population.</p>
				<p>To support the campaign last October, Ecolab provided more than 1,500 liters of hand soaps and hand sanitizers while Danone-AQUA distributed these hygiene products through local governments and communities. The distribution covered 12 target locations: Mekarsari, Langkat, Brastagi, Solok, Tanggamus, Ciherang Bogor, Babakan Pari, Citeureup, Subang, Cianjur, Kebon Candi and Pandaan. Danone-AQUA accompanied the products with instructions on proper hand hygiene as well.</p>
				<p>Allan Yong, Senior VP and Managing Director of Ecolab, Southeast Asia says, "We are proud to be working with Danone-AQUA to support our communities. We want to bring more  awareness around the importance of proper hand hygiene.” </p>
